    {
      "text": "Okay, so I hit my toe the other day and I swear there's no pain like it. I was just walking around minding my business and bam, I slammed it right into the corner of the bed. For a good five seconds, I completely lost it. I froze. I didn't even breathe. My soul literally left my body. You know that kind of pain that makes you rethink your life choices? That was me. I'm standing there holding my foot like that's gonna help, whispering things I probably shouldn't say out loud. The worst part? There's no one to blame. The bed didn't move. It's been there forever. I just forgot how to walk in my own house. And then after all that drama, I start laughing because really what else can you do? I'm there half in pain, half embarrassed, like did I seriously just injure myself doing nothing? Anyway, my toe survived barely but now every time I walk past that bed, I give it this little side-eye like not today, buddy.",
      "start_time": 0.079,
      "end_time": 67.059,
      "speaker": {
